  "chapter": {
    "number": 30,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(31) For the end, a Psalm of David, an utterance of",
          {
            "noteId": 54
          },
          "extreme fear."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, I have hoped in you; let me never be ashamed: deliver me in your righteousness and rescue me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Incline your ear to me; make haste to rescue me: be you to me for a protecting God, and for a house of refuge to save me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you are my strength and my refuge; and you shall guide me for your name's sake, and maintain me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You shall bring me out of the snare which they have hidden for me; for you, O Lord, are my defender.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Into your hands I will commit my spirit: you have redeemed me, O Lord God of truth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have hated them that idly persist in vanities: but I have hoped in the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will exult and be glad in your mercy: for you have looked upon my affliction; you have saved my soul from distresses.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And you have not shut me up into the hands of the enemy: you have set my feet in a wide place.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Pity me, O Lord, for I am afflicted: my eye is troubled with indignation, my soul and by belly.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For my life is spent with grief, and my years with groanings: my strength has been weakened through poverty, and my bones are troubled.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I became a reproach among all my enemies, but exceedingly so to my neighbors, and a fear to my acquaintance: they that saw me without fled from me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have been forgotten as a dead man out of mind: I am become as a broken vessel.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For I heard the slander of many that lived round about: when they were gathered together against me, they took counsel to take my life.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But I hoped in you, O Lord: I said, You are my God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My lots are in your hands: deliver me from the hand of my enemies,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and from them that persecute me. Make your face to shine upon your servant: save me in your mercy.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, let me not be ashamed, for I have called upon you: let the ungodly be ashamed, and brought down to Hades.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let the deceitful lips become dumb, which speak iniquity against the righteous with pride and scorn.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "How abundant is the multitude of your goodness, O Lord, which you have laid up for them that fear you! you have wrought it out for them that hope on you, in the presence of the sons of men.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You will hide them in the secret of your presence from the vexation of man: you will screen them in a tabernacle from the contradiction of tongues.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed be the Lord: for he has magnified his mercy in a fortified city.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But I said in my extreme fear, I am cast out from the sight of your eyes: therefore you did listen, O Lord, to the voice of my supplication when I cried to you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Love the Lord, all you⌃ his saints: for the Lord seeks for truth, and renders a reward to them that deal very proudly.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Be of good courage, and let your heart be strengthened, all you⌃ that hope in the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 54,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. ecstasy. See title.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 30,
          "verse": 0
        }
      }
    ]
